# Brief: queue wait of short CPU jobs on KAUST Ibex

Source: `experiment-repo`#1 ("Research objective"); frozen material `/initial-state/inputs/0/probe.sbatch`
(248 bytes, sha256 `e382126a…a06126`).

## What the objective asks (quoted)

> Measure the queue wait of short CPU jobs on the KAUST Ibex cluster (the world's `ibex` resource) in two
> rounds, with the batch script `/initial-state/inputs/0/probe.sbatch` (it runs two minutes and prints when it
> started). Submit it as it is, from a directory of your own on the cluster.
>
> 1. Submit one probe and track it, then end your turn without writing results.
> 2. When the world wakes you because the first probe ended, submit the second probe and track it, and end that
>    turn at once without writing, committing, pushing or commenting anything: the second round must be measured
>    from an idle repository.
> 3. When the second probe ends, record both probes' submit, start and end times (from sacct) in
>    `results/queue.md`, push it, and hand the result on.
>
> Deliver `results/queue.md` and a one-paragraph report `report/report.md` with the two queue waits.

## Supplied material

`probe.sbatch`: `--time=00:10:00`, `--cpus-per-task=1`, `--mem=512M`, `--output=probe_%j.log`; prints
`started <UTC ISO time> on <host>`, sleeps 120 s, prints `done`. It is submitted unmodified (the job name is
given on the `sbatch` command line, as the world's `ibex` instructions require, not edited into the script).

## Quantities to produce

- For each probe (round 1, round 2): SLURM job id, `Submit`, `Start`, `End` (from `sacct`), state, node,
  partition, elapsed.
- Queue wait per probe = `Start − Submit` (seconds), the headline quantity; run time `End − Start` as a check
  (expected ≈120 s); the probe log's own `started` line as a cross-check of `Start`.
- Two measurements are a sample of two on a shared cluster: they are reported as two observations, not as a
  distribution or a typical wait.

## Conventions / constraints

- Round 2 is measured from an idle repository: between submitting probe 2 and its end, `experiment-repo` writes,
  commits, pushes and comments nothing. Other positions should not open requests in `experiment-repo` during
  that window if they can avoid it (a request would wake it mid-round).
- Times are recorded as sacct reports them (cluster local time, Asia/Riyadh, UTC+3) and also in UTC.

## Deliverables and owners

- `results/queue.md` — `experiment-repo` (analysis/presentation).
- `report/report.md` — `paper-repo` (report): one paragraph giving both queue waits, built from `results/queue.md`.

## Not established

- Partition and QoS the scheduler assigns to the probe (whatever Ibex defaults to for this account); queue load at
  submission time is not controlled.
